Z||000000||FieroLisa||12-13-2000||10:07 PM||||Here's the deal. I would love it if I could get my gauges to light up a different color than orange. The gauges themselves are fine the color they are, but I want a different lighting, namely purple. Now, I've had the speedo apart and seen the bright orange plate back there- Is there any way to turn it to purple and get a (bright and visible) purple glow?<BR>I will have my entire GT interior apart this winter so if it can be done, this would be the time!<P><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>*Lots of New Pics!* <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||KRMFiero||12-13-2000||10:11 PM||||I have neever took apart my Fiero's Dash... (It seems the fiero is alot different then every other car made) but for my Escort I put blue lights behind it by going to Autozone with the old bulbs and they showed me exactly what ones to buy<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE<BR>Front - AudioBahn 4 x 10<BR>Headrest - AudioBahn 3 1/2<P> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||tex||12-13-2000||11:10 PM||||I had noticed that too.  I thought painting that orange plate some other fluorescent color might do it.  I have a 85 mph cluster left over from my coupe after the v6 upgrade and guage swap.  I am going to experiment on it when I can find the time. <BR>If you figue it out, let me know.  I love my Fiero but I am not fond of the orange lighting on the guages.||||reg||7
Z||000003||btoth||12-14-2000||12:41 AM||||those are 164 bulbs right?  they make other colors of them then just white... i put red ones for the interior lights under the dash.  what if you put blue lights behind the guages... blue + red makes purple right?  maybe the orange is too orange though, i don't know.  just an idea.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
